A||N||3||RiceBurner515||Cooling Fan not working||||1||
Z||000000||RiceBurner515||11-13-2000||11:40 PM||||where exactly and how many coolant temp sensors are there? My fan doesn't kick on and my engine just overheats. Could it be the fan switch/relay? where exactly is that though? How much do these sensors/switches usually go for?||||reg||1
Z||000001||RiceBurner515||11-13-2000||11:41 PM||||by the way....i have a 85 SE 4cyl.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ROB MAC||11-14-2000||07:19 PM||||<BR>The sender is on the engine block near the dipstick. It could be on top or pointing toward the driver depending on who replaced them last.<BR>Follow the fan wires and you will find the relay.<BR>If you pull the single wire connector from the sender and ground it to the engine block (key is on , car not running) the fan should run.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-14-2000||07:47 PM||||84-86 4 cyl has 3 coolant sensors.<P>the one in the thermostat neck is the ECM sensor<P>there's one with 2 green wires that is the gauge/meter sender.<P>there's another with one or 2 wires for the fan. (Only a few 84's are suposed to have the 2 wire fan sender for the 2 speed fan.) The single speed fan, which is what you should have, doesn't activate until 235F.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-14-2000).]||||reg||1
